  "script": "Crypto exchange Binance lost six point three billion dollars to hackers. That's the biggest crypto theft on record, according to Al Jazeera. It hit Thursday, and Binance paused withdrawals on several networks. Blockchain firm TRM Labs blames North Korean hackers. The old record was one point five billion, at Bybit last year. Here's what it means if you hold crypto. Binance says user funds are safe and it will cover losses. It says about two and a half billion dollars has been frozen. Where do you keep your coins: an exchange, or your own wallet? Tell us below.",
